---
import Base from '../../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import UaeGratuityCalculator from '../../../../components/UaeGratuityCalculator';
import { gratuityRules } from '../../../../calc/ae/gratuity';
import '../../../../styles/uae-gratuity.css';
---
<Base title="UAE Gratuity Calculator — Limited Beta | CalcsDesk" description="Explore a limited traditional gratuity estimate for supported foreign full-time federal private-sector workers in the UAE. Review service bands, sources and exclusions." breadcrumb="Gratuity calculator" ancestors={[{ label: 'United Arab Emirates', href: '/ae/' }]} developmentMessage="UAE calculator beta · Human review and official worked examples pending" application={{ name: 'UAE Gratuity Calculator — Limited Beta', description: 'A limited traditional gratuity illustration using entered basic wage and counted service days. Cap-affected cases excluded pending review.' }}>
  <header class="uae-page-intro"><p class="eyebrow">United Arab Emirates / End of service</p><h1>Gratuity.<br /> <span class="accent">Show the service bands.</span></h1><p class="lead">A limited traditional-gratuity estimate for foreign full-time, monthly-paid workers under the federal private-sector framework. Enter basic wage and service days to see the working. This beta does not cover every employment arrangement or determine your final settlement.</p><p class="uae-beta-line"><strong>Beta · Human review pending.</strong> Two suitable official worked examples are also pending. Cap-affected cases are excluded while conflicting official wording is reviewed. <a href="#uae-sources">Read the source and scope notes ↓</a></p></header>
  <UaeGratuityCalculator client:load />
  <noscript><section class="uae-section"><h2>JavaScript is needed for interactive results.</h2><p>The method, scope and source notes remain readable below. Enable JavaScript to enter wage and service figures.</p></section></noscript>
  <section class="uae-section" aria-labelledby="uae-scope-title"><p class="eyebrow">Check the scope first</p><h2 id="uae-scope-title">One employment model.</h2><p>{gratuityRules.scope} It uses a 365-day year and a 30-day month for this calculation. Unpaid absence is removed from entered calendar service days.</p><ul><li>Excluded cases: {gratuityRules.excluded.join('; ')}. These are limits of this tool, not statements that those workers have no entitlement.</li><li>Other settlement amounts, outstanding salary, leave payments, notice, contractual enhancements, disputes and lawful deductions are outside the result.</li><li>Date-range counting is not automated. Confirm continuous service, the correct counted service days and the applicable basic wage from your employment records.</li><li>Where the service-band accrual exceeds 24 months of basic wage, this beta shows no estimate pending cap clarification. That exclusion does not mean no gratuity is payable.</li></ul></section>
  <section class="uae-section" aria-labelledby="uae-method-title"><p class="eyebrow">Understand the number</p><h2 id="uae-method-title">Count service, then apply each band.</h2><p>Counted service equals entered calendar service days minus unpaid absence. Fewer than 365 counted days produces no gratuity in this model. For at least one counted year, the first five years accrue at 21 days of basic wage per year; later years accrue at 30 days per year. Partial years are proportional after the minimum service requirement is met.</p><p>Monthly basic wage divided by 30 gives the daily basic wage. Counted days divided by 365 gives service years. The result shows each band separately. This formula alone does not resolve eligibility, exceptions or a disputed settlement.</p><p><strong>Cap interpretation remains unresolved in this beta.</strong> The checked federal law and the checked MOHRE material use differing wage wording for the two-year cap. This tool avoids choosing a definition by excluding any case above the lower common calculation boundary of 24 months of basic wage. It does not publish a capped amount.</p></section>
  <section class="uae-section" aria-labelledby="uae-example-title"><p class="eyebrow">CalcsDesk illustration</p><h2 id="uae-example-title">Five counted years at AED 10,000 basic wage.</h2><p>With 1,825 entered service days and no unpaid absence, counted service is five years. The first band is 5 × 21 × (AED 10,000 ÷ 30) = AED 35,000. There are no later-band years in this illustration.</p><p>This is our illustration of the model, not a government-authored worked example. The required official-example and human-review checks remain pending.</p></section>
  <section id="uae-sources" class="uae-section" aria-labelledby="uae-sources-title"><p class="eyebrow">Look behind the result</p><h2 id="uae-sources-title">Source review and release status.</h2><p>Source-check record: <time datetime={gratuityRules.verified_on}>{gratuityRules.verified_on}</time>. {gratuityRules.verified_by}. A source check is distinct from human or professional review. This searchable beta has incomplete review and official-example gates; search eligibility is not verification.</p><ul>{gratuityRules.sources.map(source => <li><a href={source.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{source.title} ↗<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a><p>{source.supports}</p></li>)}</ul><p>The English Decree-Law PDF is an older publication, is not an official translation and does not establish that all provisions are consolidated through the source-check date. Arabic prevails. The MOHRE annex was available only as a search excerpt during this check; its full wording and applicability remain unverified.</p><p>Official worked examples verified: {gratuityRules.official_worked_examples.verified} of {gratuityRules.official_worked_examples.required} required. Local test illustrations do not satisfy that gate. Human review and cap clarification remain pending.</p></section>
  <section class="uae-section" aria-labelledby="uae-faq-title"><h2 id="uae-faq-title">Before you use this estimate.</h2><details><summary>Is this my complete end-of-service settlement?</summary><p>No. The displayed amount covers only the supported traditional-gratuity calculation. It excludes other entitlements, contractual terms and deductions, and does not decide a dispute.</p></details><details><summary>Why can a long service period show no result?</summary><p>Cap-affected cases are excluded pending clarification of conflicting official source wording. The tool hides the estimate and explains the unsupported case. It does not replace it with zero.</p></details><details><summary>Are my wage inputs sent anywhere?</summary><p>This calculator runs in your browser and has no submission endpoint. It does not save or share your wage or service inputs.</p></details><details><summary>Why does this beta ask for days instead of dates?</summary><p>The formula uses an explicit count of service days and unpaid absence. Automated date inclusivity and service-period interpretation have not been established for this beta, so the tool does not infer those choices.</p></details></section>
  <nav class="uae-related" aria-label="Related pages"><a href="/ae/">United Arab Emirates tools ↗</a><a href="/methodology/">How we test ↗</a><a href="/sources/">Source directory ↗</a></nav>
</Base>
